--[[
	PortalBridge - universal client script
	=========================================================================
	One file, run by BOTH players. There is no host and no guest: each client
	is authoritative over its own character and its own shots, and mirrors the
	other player's over the relay.

	Studio -> executor, what moved where:
	  ServerStorage.PortalGunModel      -> buildGun(), at runtime
	  StarterPack.PortalGun             -> a Tool made client side, into Backpack
	  PortalGunAim UnreliableRemoteEvent -> the relay's `a` frame, 30 Hz
	  Character attr PortalGunAim       -> peer.aim, applied to a local C0
	  PortalGunService grip + aim       -> rigOf() + poseStep()
	  PortalService portals + travel    -> local, driven by `s` / `c` / `t`
	  PortalGunAimClient                -> poseStep(), now for both characters
	  PortalVisualsClient               -> visualStep()
	  StarterGui.Cursor                 -> buildCursor()

	R6 and R15 both. The aim rotates the right shoulder in either rig; the gun
	grips the R6 "Right Arm" or the R15 "RightHand". Same joint algebra either
	way:
	    part1.CFrame = part0.CFrame * C0 * Transform * C1:Inverse()
	The Animator owns Transform and rewrites it every frame, so every pose here
	goes through C0 with that frame's Transform cancelled back out of it, on
	PreSimulation. Nothing this script writes replicates - which is the whole
	reason the relay exists.

	The VIP-server gate is OFF (CONFIG.REQUIRE_VIP). PrivateServerId and
	PrivateServerOwnerId are Not Replicated: a client reads "" and 0, so the check
	can only ever refuse, and the relay cannot verify them either - whatever the
	client sends is what it read, which is nothing. What does hold today is the
	relay's token, its place allowlist, and its requirement that both players
	report the same JobId. See README, "The VIP gate, and why it is off".
]]

